## Analysis of Failures

All 9 failures share one root cause: **path components are being concatenated without `/` separators**. Evidence:
- `a/b/c/d` → created `abcd` instead of `a/b/c/d`
- `p/./q` → created `pq` instead of `p/q`
- `link/child` → created `linkchild` instead of `link/child`
- `ro/child/grandchild` → created `rochildgrandchild` (succeeding in the writable top-level dir) instead of failing with EACCES inside the read-only `ro/`

The `fault-readonly-parent-with-p` failure is a direct consequence: the slash-less path `rochildgrandchild` is created at the top level (writable) instead of inside `ro/` (read-only), so it exits 0 instead of 1.

## Root Cause

The current `mkdir_p` builds the path via `OsString::push` in a component loop, but the resulting paths clearly lack separators. The fix is to build the path explicitly as a `Vec<u8>` with manually inserted `/` bytes, eliminating any ambiguity in separator handling.

